# Overpass responses and derived build products — all regenerable, and large.
# The hand-maintained files are NOT ignored.
#
# All three lines are load-bearing, in this order (same as citybrowser/cityhistory):
#
#   !data/   the REPO ROOT .gitignore excludes `data/` as a directory, and git does
#            not descend into an excluded directory — so without this, no negation
#            below can reach anything inside and the hand-maintained roster stays
#            silently untracked.
#   data/*   re-exclude the CONTENTS, as children rather than as a directory, which
#            is what leaves the next lines reachable.
#   !...     the exceptions that actually matter.
#
# Verify after any edit — the failure mode here is silence, not an error. Use the
# EXIT CODE, not the output: `-v` prints the matching rule even when that rule is a
# negation, so a printed line does not mean the file is ignored.
#   git check-ignore -q neighborhoods/data/cities_seed.csv   # must exit 1 (not ignored)
#   git check-ignore -q neighborhoods/data/base.json         # must exit 0 (ignored)
!data/
data/*
!data/cities_seed.csv
!data/levels_override.json
!data/tier_map.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- machine transfer
# TRACKED SO THE WORK CAN MOVE BETWEEN MACHINES. Everything below is regenerable in
# principle and ruinous to regenerate in practice — together these are ~15 hours of
# fetching and ~1.4 GB of downloads, in ~143 MB of files.
#
# The rule for what belongs here: track the DISTILLATE, never the cache it came from.
# build.py reads only these data/*.json files; it never opens cache/kontur (881 MB),
# cache/wof (521 MB) or cache/external (19 MB). Those three exist solely to produce the
# four small files below and can be deleted without affecting a build.
#
#   kontur_pop.json      0.7 MB  <- 881 MB of downloads
#   wof_shapes.json     12.8 MB  <- 521 MB
#   external_shapes.json 6.6 MB  <-  19 MB
#   wiki.json            3.0 MB  <- the sitelinks pass
#
# NOT derived output. base.json, units/, geom/ and city_shapes.json stay ignored: they
# rebuild from the caches below in about three minutes, and they change every build.
!data/wof_shapes.json
!data/external_shapes.json
!data/wiki.json
!data/kontur_pop.json
!data/p31.json
!data/pop.json
!data/city_area.json
!data/city_candidates.json

# Overpass cache: one JSON per city per pass. Regenerable, but slowly and at
# someone else's expense — do not delete casually.
#
# Same directory trap as data/ above: git will not descend into an excluded directory,
# so `!cache/` has to come first or no negation below it can reach anything.
!cache/
cache/*
# survey (74 MB) and boundary (32 MB) are the Overpass passes worth carrying. Boundary is
# the slow one despite its size: 38% of cities miss the QID match and cost three requests
# including a global is_in() lookup (spec 8).
!cache/survey/
!cache/boundary/
# views.jsonl is the ~6.5 h pageviews pass and is append-only; sitelinks.jsonl is read
# directly by build.py as a ledger supplement.
!cache/wiki/
#
# cache/geom is DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. It is 527 MB and covers only 61 of 287 cities, and
# the geometry pass has to be re-run for the other 226 anyway — refetching 61 alongside
# them is noise. Move it out of band if you want it, but do not put it in git.
cache/geom/
